# UMBP IOBW Benchmark — Known-Good Environment

These values are taken from runs that actually PASSED in the transcript history.
**Never invent a MODEL_PATH.** The default `/nfs/data/DeepSeek-V3` in
`tools/iobw/run_umbp_iobw_test.sh` is WRONG on the skyriver07 box (no config.json there).

## Tiers & which case to run (READ THIS FIRST)

Hierarchy: **L1 = HBM (device)**, **L2 = host DRAM** (`--hicache-size` /
`MLATokenToKVPoolHost`), **L3 = UMBP storage backend** (UMBP DRAM tier and/or SSD tier).

- The **default / primary test is DRAM-only L3: L3 DRAM -> L2 DRAM -> HBM. NO SPDK/SSD.**
- bench cases (`run_tiered_cache_bench_dp8ep8.sh`):
  - `case1:HBM_Only`  = L1 only (no hierarchical cache).
  - `case2:HBM_DRAM`  = L1 + L2 host DRAM, **NO UMBP / NO L3** (just `--enable-hierarchical-cache`).
  - `case3:HBM_DRAM_SSD` = L1 + L2 + **L3 UMBP**. This is the ONLY case that exercises UMBP.
- To test the **L3 DRAM tier WITHOUT SSD/SPDK**: use `case3` but disable SSD:
  - `UMBP_SSD_BYTES=0`  -> `ssd_enabled=false` (L3 = UMBP DRAM tier only).
  - `UMBP_SSD_BACKEND=posix` (default) -> bench injects NO `spdk_*` fields
    (it only adds them when backend != posix; see launch_server_case3 L441).
  - `UMBP_DRAM_BYTES` sets the L3 DRAM tier capacity (default 64 GB/rank).
- Only set `UMBP_SSD_BACKEND=spdk_proxy` + `UMBP_SPDK_NVME_PCI` + `UMBP_SPDK_PROXY_BIN`
  + `UMBP_SSD_BYTES>0` when you explicitly want the SSD/SPDK tier. Passing those in a
  DRAM-only run is what caused the bogus `spdk_nvme_pci_addr` path.

### To MEASURE L3 READ bandwidth (BatchGet): use READ_REPLAY=true

Without it you only get writes (`BatchPut`), because reused prefixes still hit
L1/L2 and never read L3 -> `BatchGet=0`. The ready-made mechanism is
`READ_REPLAY=true` (`run_tiered_cache_bench_dp8ep8.sh` L372-396 ->
`bench_multiturn.py:run_read_replay`): after the write phase it calls
`/flush_cache` (wipes HBM + host DRAM, **L3 storage tier survives**), then
replays the same prompts so the prefix match misses L1/L2 and is served from
L3 -> forces `batch_get_v1` BatchGet. **Always set `READ_REPLAY=true` when you
want read bandwidth.** Do NOT try to force eviction by shrinking L2 below the
27 GB device floor.

### DRAM-only one-shot command (L3 DRAM -> L2 -> HBM)

```bash
cd /sgl-workspace/sglang && \
MODEL_PATH=/mnt/nvme1/data/DeepSeekV3.1 \
UMBP_LOG_LEVEL=0 CASES_OVERRIDE=case3:HBM_DRAM_SSD DUMMY_FORWARD=true \
NUM_ROUNDS=40 NUM_CLIENTS=1 MAX_PARALLEL=1 HICACHE_SIZE=32 \
UMBP_SSD_BACKEND=posix UMBP_SSD_BYTES=0 \
DO_CHECKOUT=false tools/iobw/run_umbp_iobw_test.sh 2>&1 | tee /tmp/iobw_run.log; \
echo "==================== IOBW RESULT (inline) ====================" && \
RDIR="$(ls -1dt benchmark/hicache/results/tiered_cache_bench_dp8ep8/*/ 2>/dev/null | head -n1 | sed 's:/$::')" && \
{ [ -n "$RDIR" ] && echo "results_dir = $RDIR" && \
  ( python3 tools/iobw/summarize_iobw_jsonl.py "$RDIR"/**/iobw_*.jsonl 2>/dev/null \
    || bash tools/iobw/diagnose_iobw_logs.sh "$RDIR" 2>&1 | grep -E "bandwidth|GiB/s|avg|max|count|IOBW" ) \
  || echo "NO DATA: see /tmp/iobw_run.log"; }
```

