## Prerequisite: hugepages (run inside container, privileged)

Each of 8 DP ranks needs ~7.45 GB DRAM-tier hugepage + proxy needs node0 headroom.
Set both NUMA nodes to 32 GB each (64 GB total) BEFORE the bench, or spdk_proxy
EAL fails to grab node0 memory:

```bash
echo 16384 > /sys/devices/system/node/node0/hugepages/hugepages-2048kB/nr_hugepages
echo 16384 > /sys/devices/system/node/node1/hugepages/hugepages-2048kB/nr_hugepages
grep HugePages_Total /proc/meminfo   # expect 32768
```

## Known-good one-shot command (read-bandwidth case3)

Small L2 (`HICACHE_SIZE=8`) forces eviction to L3, prefix reuse triggers BatchGet
(read bandwidth). Per the inline-results rule, end with the bandwidth summary printed.

```bash
cd /sgl-workspace/sglang && \
MODEL_PATH=/mnt/nvme1/data/DeepSeekV3.1 \
UMBP_SSD_BACKEND=spdk_proxy UMBP_SPDK_NVME_PCI=0000:88:00.0 \
UMBP_SPDK_PROXY_BIN=/opt/venv/lib/python3.10/site-packages/mori/spdk_proxy \
UMBP_LOG_LEVEL=0 CASES_OVERRIDE=case3:HBM_DRAM_SSD DUMMY_FORWARD=true \
NUM_ROUNDS=40 NUM_CLIENTS=1 MAX_PARALLEL=1 HICACHE_SIZE=8 \
DO_CHECKOUT=false tools/iobw/run_umbp_iobw_test.sh 2>&1 | tee /tmp/iobw_run.log; \
echo "==================== IOBW RESULT (inline) ====================" && \
RDIR="$(ls -1dt benchmark/hicache/results/tiered_cache_bench_dp8ep8/*/ 2>/dev/null | head -n1 | sed 's:/$::')" && \
{ [ -n "$RDIR" ] && echo "results_dir = $RDIR" && \
  ( python3 tools/iobw/summarize_iobw_jsonl.py "$RDIR"/**/iobw_*.jsonl 2>/dev/null \
    || bash tools/iobw/diagnose_iobw_logs.sh "$RDIR" 2>&1 | grep -E "bandwidth|GiB/s|avg|max|count|IOBW" ) \
  || echo "NO DATA: see /tmp/iobw_run.log"; }
```

If launched from the **host** shell, wrap with:
`docker exec storge bash -lc "<command above>"`

## HARD CONSTRAINT: HICACHE_SIZE must exceed the device KV pool

`memory_pool_host.py` asserts `host_pool.size > device_pool.size`
("The host memory should be larger than the device memory with the current
protocol"). `HICACHE_SIZE` (GB) is converted to tokens via
`HICACHE_SIZE*1e9 / size_per_token`, and that must exceed `device_pool.size`.

Measured on skyriver07 / DeepSeekV3.1 / default mem-fraction:
- device KV pool per rank = **27.04 GB / 413056 tokens** (`KV Cache is allocated. #tokens: 413056, KV size: 27.04 GB`).
- Therefore **`HICACHE_SIZE` must be > 27.04 GB**. `HICACHE_SIZE=8` crashes every
  scheduler with the AssertionError (parent then dies with `EOFError` from the
  scheduler pipe). **Use `HICACHE_SIZE=32` (known-good).**
- To still force eviction into L3 (to capture read bandwidth via BatchGet), do NOT
  shrink L2 below the floor — instead drive a larger working set: more rounds /
  longer prompts / more clients, or lower the device mem-fraction to drop the floor.

## VERIFIED-PASSED command + result (banff, 2026-05-29)

This exact shape PASSED end-to-end (case3, DUMMY_FORWARD):
`NUM_ROUNDS=20 NUM_CLIENTS=1 MAX_PARALLEL=1 HICACHE_SIZE=32`, write_through,
L2=32GB/rank, L3 DRAM=64GB/rank, L3 SSD=96GB/rank, backend=spdk_proxy.

Result (recomputed from JSONL, source of truth):
- BatchPut: 26 calls / 656 requests, 2.75 GiB written, **avg 1.405 GiB/s**
  (p50 1.32 / p95 1.85 / max 1.86 GiB/s); batch ~137 MiB; per-call 75-106 ms.
- **BatchGet = 0**: fresh cache is write-only on first pass. To measure READ
  bandwidth you must run enough rounds with prefix reuse so data is read back
  from L3 (BatchGet). Plan for multi-round + small-enough L2-vs-workingset.

## mori config refactor: spdk_* fields are NESTED under cfg.ssd

New mori `UMBPConfig` exposes all SPDK fields on `UMBPSsdConfig`
(pybind: `pybind_umbp.cpp` ~L154-185), i.e. `cfg.ssd.spdk_*`, NOT top-level.
Symptom if you use the old flat path:
`AttributeError: 'libmori_pybinds.UMBPConfig' object has no attribute 'spdk_nvme_pci_addr'`
(scheduler dies -> parent `EOFError` from scheduler pipe).

Fixed in `umbp_store.py`: every `cfg.spdk_*` / `cfg.spdk_proxy_*` ->
`cfg.ssd.spdk_*` (and `getattr(cfg, "spdk_proxy_*")` -> `getattr(cfg.ssd, ...)`).
`cfg.ssd.ssd_backend` was already nested. If a fresh checkout reintroduces flat
`cfg.spdk_*`, re-apply this nesting fix.

## Health markers to watch
`spdk_proxy: READY` -> `UMBPStore initialized ... ssd_backend=spdk_proxy` ->
`Server is ready` -> `BatchPut done ... bandwidth_gib_s` ->
(after enough rounds) `BatchGet done ... bandwidth_gib_s` (= read BW) -> `PASSED`.
